{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_449","type":"reasoning","text":"Interesting: docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/l03-*.md and .json are ignored by `.gitignore` (/docs/** ignored). But wait — the harness validate ownership gate uses `getChangedFiles` which includes untracked files via `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard`, which honors .gitignore. So the docs files aren't seen as changed files? Let me check. Actually in the L01/L02 records, docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/*.md and *.json ARE in targetScope. And in the historical result for L01, the diff \"added\" included docs files. So they must be tracked somehow.\n\nActually the .gitignore has `!/docs/**/` which un-ignores directories but not files. Hmm, `/docs/**` ignores everything, `!/docs/**/` re-includes directories. That means files directly under an un-ignored dir... Actually git semantics: if a directory is excluded, git won't descend. `!/docs/**/` negates directories. Then files inside are not re-included by `!/docs/**/`, so files remain excluded. But `git ls-files --others` shows only the two ts/md files as untracked, meaning the docs files ARE ignored.\n\nBut the harness validate ownership gate passed with only those two files. Let me check: the harness validate returned \"Spec is valid\" and computed ownership over changedFiles. Since docs files are ignored (not in untracked list), they're not in changedFiles, so no ownership failure. That's fine but means docs aren't part of the \"change set\" seen by the harness. In L01's case the docs were added to the trial diff, so the harness must have required them. Let me verify how the trial's diff collector works — it likely copies the whole workspace and diffs against base, ignoring .gitignore? Let me check the L01 historical diff: added docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/L01-SHA256SUMS etc. So the trial diff DOES include docs files despite .gitignore. That means their diff tool doesn't honor .gitignore, or these doc paths are force-added.\n\nActually looki